            "content": "# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Project\n\nkxo is a Linux kernel module implementing a tic-tac-toe game engine that runs entirely in kernel space. Two AI players (MCTS vs Negamax) compete autonomously. A userspace companion tool (`xo-user`) reads the game state via `/dev/kxo` and renders it in the terminal.\n\n## Build Commands\n\n```bash\nmake              # Build kernel module (kxo.ko) + userspace tool (xo-user)\nmake kmod         # Build kernel module only\nmake xo-user      # Build userspace tool only\nmake clean        # Clean all build artifacts\n```\n\nRequires kernel headers at `/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build`. First build installs git hooks via `scripts/install-git-hooks`.\n\n## Load / Run / Unload\n\n```bash\nsudo insmod kxo.ko      # Load module\nsudo ./xo-user           # Run visualization (Ctrl+P pause, Ctrl+Q quit)\nsudo rmmod kxo           # Unload module\n```\n\n## Code Style\n\n- clang-format with `.clang-format` (Chromium-based, 4-space indent, no tabs)\n- Pre-commit hook enforces: clang-format, cppcheck static analysis, aspell spelling, banned function check (gets, sprintf, strcpy, etc.)\n- Commit messages validated by `scripts/commit-msg.hook`\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Threading Model\n\nTimer (softirq, 100ms) -> Tasklet (bottom-half) -> Workqueue (kernel threads)\n\nThe timer fires periodically, schedules a tasklet that checks game state, and the tasklet queues work items onto `kxo_workqueue`:\n- `ai_one_work` - MCTS player ('O', 100k iterations)\n- `ai_two_work` - Negamax player ('X', alpha-beta + PVS, depth 6)\n- `drawboard_work` - Renders board to circular buffer\n\n### Synchronization\n\n- `producer_lock` / `consumer_lock` mutexes serialize kfifo writes and workqueue access\n- `rwlock_t` on `kxo_attr` for sysfs attribute access\n- `kfifo` (lock-free) for kernel-to-userspace data transfer\n- `circ_buf` for interrupt-context board state transfer\n- `local_irq_disable`/`enable` guards around circular buffer access\n- Memory barriers (`smp_rmb`/`smp_wmb`) for circular buffer coherence\n\n### Game Board\n\n4x4 grid, 3-in-a-row to win (`BOARD_SIZE=4`, `GOAL=3`, defined in `game.h`). Fixed-point arithmetic (8-bit fractional) for score calculations.\n\n### AI Algorithms\n\n- **MCTS** (`mcts.c`): UCT selection, random rollout via xoroshiro128++ PRNG, 100k iterations per move\n- **Negamax** (`negamax.c`): Alpha-beta pruning, PVS, iterative deepening (depths 2/4/6), move ordering via history heuristic\n- **Zobrist** (`zobrist.c`): Transposition table (hash size 100003) using wyhash64-seeded random values, kernel hlist chaining\n\n### Device Interface\n\n`main.c` registers char device `/dev/kxo` with open/read/poll/release ops. Sysfs attributes at `/sys/class/kxo/kxo/kxo_state` control pause/resume/end. `xo-user.c` uses select() to multiplex keyboard input and device reads.\n\n### Kernel Version Compatibility\n\n`main.c` has `KERNEL_VERSION` guards for API differences in kernels 6.4 and 6.12+ (tasklet API, class_create signature, no_llseek removal).\n",
